Recursion 
• Functions can call themselves. 
• fib(n) = fib(n-1) + fib(n-2) can be easily 
expressed via a recursive implementation 
int fibonacci(int n) { 
  if (n == 0 || n == 1) { 
    return 1; 
  } else { 
    return fibonacci(n-2) + fibonacci(n-1); 
  } 
}

